{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "Scope placement changes executable answers. node.2a6321b4ce90763bf0be564e puts offering in Scope; node.6d6e7adc6faa9d94b74c08e5, node.968dbccb08282a4e8a580ae5, node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f and node.bca408c75cbf8467afafada6 put promotional linkage in Scope. Failed conditions return OUT_OF_SCOPE rather than FALSE for prohibition questions or TRUE for selected-control compliance. Deliberate applicability boundaries remain a possible interpretation, but their agreement with the typed questions is unresolved.",
    "The offer-level candidates combine an offer-level promotional link with an existential non-discount gift component. Establish that the qualifying gift itself bears the required promotional connection; otherwise facts about unrelated components could produce an unsupported prohibition.",
    "Unit db43e253bea18.u0.2 defines distributors through distribution of SFC-authorised funds. Broader distributor wording in some candidates needs that contextual limitation. Conversely, node.97af37a2579f59b0ee43211f narrows the promoted specific product to an SFC-authorised fund, while u13.2987 says 'specific investment product'. Whether this is contextual scoping or an unsupported exclusion remains unresolved.",
    "Code of Conduct paragraph 3.11 and question 1 of the SFC FAQs issued on 30 September 2010, identified in footnote 3, are missing external authorities. Can their applicable texts be supplied to check qualifications and gift classifications? No dependency IDs are supplied; the circular's express summary remains supported.",
    "Unit db43e253bea18.u12.2646 says returns and incentives may be gifts; it does not classify all incentives automatically. Unit db43e253bea18.u7.1360 distinguishes fund return from distributor top-up. Component classifications must preserve these distinctions, and a discount in one component cannot exempt a distinct non-discount gift.",
    "A discount exception or TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT answers only the selected gift control. It does not establish compliance with section 103 or paragraph 2.3. Neither structured-product status nor section 103 authorisation is a prerequisite or exception to the gift test.",
    "The supplied source does not establish the candidates' asserted operative date interval. Runtime uncertainty handling does not establish the applicable legal version.",
    "Node.bc55be7e973a689d07f9e64b requires offer attribution, consistently with the source's offering trigger. Its categorical funding and fulfilment independence is not expressly resolved by the source; third-party attribution must remain assessed rather than presumed."
  ],
